@@ -35,7 +35,8 @@ tokens/copy from this doc win. Build with committed primitives only.
 - Hint: "Need a hint" quiet → reveals ONE hint into InsetPanel(label "HINT", ink-700) 250ms fade. Relabel "Another hint" only if a 2nd tier exists (max two, never the answer). Focus stays on Input. Hints logged (count against mastery weight, never shamed).
 - FEEDBACK MOMENT (on Submit: record, render feedback in place keeping prompt+visual, move focus to feedback region, announce aria-live polite). NEVER a bare icon.
   STATE A CORRECT: CheckIcon in 22px success-bg circle (status-mastered) + body 15/600 status-mastered "Correct". Marked-up visual: student's correct point/line drawn status-mastered green w/ mono label (or worked result in success chip). WHY (≤2 sentences, InsetPanel no label, body ink-800): template "{whatRight}. {whyItWorks}." Inform, don't celebrate (no "Great job"/"!"). Momentum +1. Primary "Next problem" (autoFocus; last item → "See your summary").
-  STATE B INCORRECT+TAG: CrossIcon in 22px error-bg circle + body 15/600 error-ink "Not quite" (never "Wrong"/"Incorrect"). MARKED-UP VISUAL (the brief's point): show BOTH — student answer as hollow/dashed marker in error-ink labeled "you" AND correct as solid status-mastered marker labeled "correct"; the gap/divergence is visible (number line: hollow-error vs solid-green; plane: dashed-error line vs solid-correct line). WHAT/WHY (InsetPanel, body ink-800): "{whatYouDid}. {theFix}." Bounded TUTOR panel: 1px border-strong radius 10, header inset bg eyebrow(label,ink-500) "TUTOR" + 14px helper glyph; Diagnosis (body ink-800) "What's happening: {tutor.diagnosis}"; Sport reframe (body ink-700) "In context: {tutor.reframe}" (absent P3); Bridge (body-sm ink-500) "{tutor.bridgeToNeutral}". Tutor explains/reframes ONLY — never "let me", no avatar, no chat bubbles, no typing animation, never routes/sets mastery. Primary "Try again" if re-attempt permitted (clears input, collapses tutor to quiet "Show the tutor again"), else "Next problem".
+  STATE B INCORRECT+TAG: CrossIcon in 22px error-bg circle + body 15/600 error-ink "Not quite" (never "Wrong"/"Incorrect"). MARKED-UP VISUAL (the brief's point): show BOTH — student answer as hollow/dashed marker in error-ink labeled "you" AND correct as solid status-mastered marker labeled "correct"; the gap/divergence is visible (number line: hollow-error vs solid-green; plane: dashed-error line vs solid-correct line). WHAT/WHY (InsetPanel, body ink-800): "{whatYouDid}. {theFix}." Bounded TUTOR panel: 1px border-strong radius 10, header inset bg eyebrow(label,ink-500) "TUTOR" + 14px helper glyph; Diagnosis (body ink-800) "What's happening: {tutor.diagnosis}"; Sport reframe (body ink-700) "In context: {tutor.reframe}" (absent P3); Bridge (body-sm ink-500) "{tutor.bridgeToNeutral}".
+  ADDENDUM (2026-06-14, binding — H2 tutor fix): the UI "In context:" bold label is REMOVED. The framing lead-in now lives INSIDE the lib `reframe` string ("The core idea for this skill: …" neutral / "The core idea, in {sport} terms: …" sport), so the panel renders `{tutor.reframe}` as a single plain ink-700 body line (no eyebrow). The neutral bridge is suppressed (`bridgeToNeutral === ""` for neutral students → renders nothing via the truthiness gate); the sport bridge keeps its quieter body-sm ink-500 treatment. `tutor.diagnosis` is NEVER rendered to a student (audit-only). Tutor explains/reframes ONLY — never "let me", no avatar, no chat bubbles, no typing animation, never routes/sets mastery. Primary "Try again" if re-attempt permitted (clears input, collapses tutor to quiet "Show the tutor again"), else "Next problem".
   STATE C INCORRECT NO TAG: same header "Not quite" + marked-up visual. WHY InsetPanel = assembled plain "why" (see spec §B; NO fabricated misconception). No tutor panel (honesty). Optional quiet "Compare your steps to the worked example, one line at a time." Primary "Try again"/"Next problem".
 - Momentum (top-right of problem card): streak-of-correct ONLY. Each correct = 7px filled accent dot (status-mastered green once streak ≥3). Miss → run resets to empty quietly (no red dot). Cap ~5 visible then "5+" micro mono ink-500. No total-correct tally, no confetti. aria-label "Correct in a row: {n}".
 - Edge: no problems → calm Card "This practice set is being prepared." + secondary "Back to the lesson". Persist failure mid-session → keep attempt in client state, feedback still renders, quiet AlertPanel bottom "We're saving your work and will retry automatically." (role=status), never lose answer. Visual fail → degrade, Input still works.
